Input: {"question": "When was Jimmy Ryan born?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d00", "start": 0, "end": 101, "text": "was spotted by a scout and invited for an initial two-week trial with English club Manchester United."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d00", "start": 102, "end": 202, "text": "The trial was extended to a month and Ryan signed as an apprentice with the club on 7 December 1962."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d00", "start": 203, "end": 405, "text": "A month later, he signed his first professional contract, but it was not until May 1966 that he made his first-team debut, playing on the right wing in the final four league games of the 1965–66 season."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d00", "start": 406, "end": 510, "text": "He scored his first goal in the third of those games, the third goal in a 6–1 home win over Aston Villa."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d00", "start": 511, "end": 535, "text": "He played for Manchester"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d01", "start": 0, "end": 615, "text": "Jimmy Ryan (footballer, born 1975) - Wikipedia Jump to content Main menu Main menu move to sidebar hide Navigation Main page Contents Current events Random article About Wikipedia Contact us Contribute Help Learn to edit Community portal Recent changes Upload file Special pages Search Search Appearance Donate Create account Log in Personal tools Donate Create account Log in Pages for logged out editors learn more Contributions Talk Contents move to sidebar hide ( Top ) 1 Playing career 2 Managerial career 3 Career statistics 4 Honours Toggle Honours subsection 4.1 Manager 5 References 6 External links Toggle"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d02", "start": 0, "end": 8, "text": "a trial."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d02", "start": 9, "end": 95, "text": "He scored his first goal for the Republic of Ireland U21 in Lithuania in October 2008."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d02", "start": 96, "end": 224, "text": "After his performances for Accrington Stanley throughout the 2010–11 League Two season he was voted in the PFA Team of the Year."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d02", "start": 225, "end": 310, "text": "On 28 June 2011 he signed a two-year contract with League One side Scunthorpe United."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d02", "start": 311, "end": 392, "text": "On 5 June 2013 Ryan signed a one-year contract with League Two side Chesterfield."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d02", "start": 393, "end": 459, "text": "On 1 July 2015, Ryan signed for Fleetwood Town on a free transfer."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d02", "start": 460, "end": 559, "text": "After 67 appearances and winning the club's Player of the Year in 2016, Ryan penned a two-year deal"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d03", "start": 0, "end": 503, "text": "birth Bolton , Lancashire , England [ 1 ] Height 6 ft 0 in ( 1.83 m ) [ 2 ] Position ( s ) Defender [ 1 ] Senior career * Years Team Apps ( Gls ) 1983–1987 Bolton Wanderers 108 ( 2 ) 1987–1988 Rangers 25 ( 0 ) 1988–1990 Oxford United 79 ( 8 ) 1990–1993 Middlesbrough 139 ( 6 ) 1993–2001 Bolton Wanderers 221 ( 3 ) Total 572 ( 19 ) Managerial career 2005–2008 Bolton Wanderers Reserves 2008–2020 Bolton Wanderers Academy 2012 Bolton Wanderers ( caretaker ) 2016 Bolton Wanderers ( caretaker ) 2019 Bolton"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d04", "start": 0, "end": 135, "text": "won two FAI Cup winners medals , First Division title in 1999/2000 and two Leinster Senior Cup runners-up medals in 1988/89 & 1989/90 ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d04", "start": 136, "end": 262, "text": "John holds the club record at Bray Wanderers for most league goals in a season when he scored 16 goals in the 1989/90 season ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d04", "start": 263, "end": 354, "text": "He also shares the record of most goals scored in a season in all competitions : 20 goals ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d04", "start": 355, "end": 465, "text": "John set the record originally in the 1988–89 season before Kieran O'Brien equalled it in the 1995–96 season ."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d04", "start": 466, "end": 532, "text": "John Ryan is Bray Wanderers fifth highest goalscorer of all time ."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d04", "start": 533, "end": 535, "text": "In"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d05", "start": 0, "end": 34, "text": "nine thousand dollars to relocate."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d05", "start": 35, "end": 76, "text": "The club was owned by partners Matthew C."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d05", "start": 77, "end": 130, "text": "(Matty) Walsh (1914–2006) and Jimmy Ryan (1911–1963)."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d05", "start": 131, "end": 245, "text": "Walsh, Ryan's brother-in-law, continued ownership following the death of Ryan in July 1963 at the French Hospital."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d05", "start": 246, "end": 256, "text": "Gilbert J."}, "D6S6": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0313-6ab15066014a:d05", "start": 257, "end": 432, "text": "Pincus (1907–1980) — who served as 